  "question": "Why do some e6b9dc5d decisions replay with the same action but a different RNG stream after, and 4 with a different action?",
  "method": "Each such decision was replayed again through the production worker runtime with the pinned store snapshots loaded, once per governor scale on the published table (1, 0.6, 0.35, 0.2, 0.08) held for every Monte Carlo read of the decision, and, had no single scale matched, with every two-scale schedule switching at every read. A scale reproduces a decision when the accepted action, the amount and the RNG state after the decision all equal the journaled ones.",
  "finding": "Every one of the decisions reproduces exactly at one or two single neighbouring scales and never at the journaled scale; no switching schedule was needed. The journaled governorScale was read after decide() returned, and EquityLoadGovernor.current() takes a new reading whenever a second has passed, so under load the journal carried a reading the decision never used.",
  "fix": "EquityLoadGovernor.withDecisionScale: read once before the decision, held for every Monte Carlo read inside it, journaled and reported as that value (commit ec15b4da on this branch). Records made before the fix keep their journaled value and replay as they are; nothing is re-scaled to make them reproduce.",
